not_done.why:
This is the spec's cut line. The review-only pass has no plan line of its own today: the generic plan line prints the planner's work estimate. The app also has no estimate for a review's cost at all. The critic is paid from the session's reserve, and only its first call's worst case is ever computed. Fixing it means:
- a new review-cost estimate (a design choice);
- marking review-only items at plan time (latestWorkRun + pendingOfRun with a matching attempt);
- changing the Start dialog's start-check too, or the plan line and the Start dialog would disagree again (R-estimates).
The Start dialog and start-check belong to other areas and run C. Suggested follow-up:
- the runner marks a plan item reviewOnly when its task holds a pending review result, with a work estimate of 0;
- session.planned carries reviewOnly titles, and the line reads 'Plan: the review of "X", whose work was done in an earlier session.' (with 'about CHF N' once a review estimate exists);
- start-check says the same.

new_problems:
A session review whose 'revise' verdict has another cause still reads 'Session review: sent back for changes' for the session. Examples:
- a cost overrun;
- a plan estimate above the session budget;
- spend without a plan.
Nothing is sent back in these cases either. Evidence: views.ts critic.session_review falls back to verdictWords('revise'); only the waits-for-you cases (answers, decision, failed with a card) got their own words here. It needs words that name the finding's kind (e.g. 'the work cost more than planned'). Words item for l3-small or a later run.

